Revision history for DBIx-Squirrel

Unreleased

    - connect croaks on failure, and clones an existing database
      handle passed in place of a data source.
    - pipe runs a list of stages as a pipeline: each stage gets what
      the one before returned, and pipe returns what the last one
      returned. A stage returning an empty list ends the pipeline;
      Stop ends it early, keeping the values reached.
    - Stop comes from DBIx::Squirrel::Stop, exported automatically. A
      stage calls Stop(...) or DBIx::Squirrel::Stop->throw(...), and
      the Stop carries the arguments given. A subclass of
      DBIx::Squirrel::Stop stops a pipeline too.
    - tap runs the same kind of pipeline as a branch off to the side,
      for its side effects, and returns its invocant.
    - A stage can be named, and a failing stage is named in the
      error.
    - The successor to 1.6.5 begins, in a fresh repository: a rewrite in
      modern Perl, requiring Perl 5.36 or later. 1.x is archived in
      https://github.com/nukopian/DBIx-Squirrel-1.
